<title>INDONESIA: Jababeka says 1996 net profit up.</title>
<headline>Jababeka says 1996 net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian industrial and housing developer PT Kawasan Industri Jababeka said on Thursday it booked a net profit of 186.5 billion rupiah in 1996 against 137.3 billion rupiah in the previous year.</p>
<p>In early March, the company said in a statement that it posted a net profit of 175 billion rupiah in 1996 but the statement gave no other details.</p>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in billion rupiah unless stated )</p>
<p>    Net profit			 186.5    vs   137.3</p>
<p>    Revenues			   547.9    vs   348.9</p>
<p>    Gross profit		     250.0    vs   169.2</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 192.5    vs   129.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   229.5    vs   187.4</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (in rph)    386    vs     438</p>
<p>    Retained earnings		341.8    vs   186.6</p>
<p>NOTE : The results were audited. PT Kawasan Industri Jababeka is a Jakarta-based firm which develops and operates industrial and housing estates.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
